    sceneNote:{ en:"The selected scenes track the prosecution's charging decisions and the defense's procedural countermoves across the bond hearing, the murder preliminary, and the recusal argument.", zh:"本集多句台词涉及（hate crime）仇恨犯罪、（misdemeanor battery）轻罪殴打、（bail）保释、（first degree murder）一级谋杀、（prosecutorial misconduct）检方不当行为、（recuse）回避、（probable cause）合理根据、（plea bargain）辩诉交易与（objection）异议等概念。剧情围绕检方加重指控、辩方以程序动议反制，以及法官卡普曼拒绝回避而展开。" },
    terms:[ "hate_crime", "misdemeanor_battery", "bail", "first_degree_murder", "prosecutorial_misconduct", "probable_cause", "recuse", "plea_bargain", "objection" ],
    uk:{ en:"Under English law there is no freestanding 'hate crime' offense; hostility toward a protected group is a sentencing aggravator under the Crime and Disorder Act 1998, not a separate charge. 'Bail' exists but is granted more restrictively. There is no 'first degree murder' -- murder carries a mandatory life sentence and manslaughter is the only lesser homicide. Recusal follows the same appearance-of-bias test (Porter v Magill). 'Plea bargain' has no formal equivalent; most cases resolve by guilty plea to the indictment as drawn. Prosecutorial misconduct is curtailed by the CPS Code and abuse-of-process stays.", zh:"在英格兰与威尔士法律下并无独立的“仇恨犯罪”罪名，针对受保护群体的敌意仅依《1998年犯罪与秩序法》作为量刑加重事由。保释制度存在但批准更审慎；没有“一级谋杀”之分，谋杀科处强制无期徒刑，过失杀人方为轻一档的杀人罪。回避同样适用“外观偏见”标准（Porter v Magill）。英国无正式“辩诉交易”，多数案件以就起诉书认罪了结。检方不当行为受皇家检控署守则约束，并可经滥用程序而中止诉讼。" }
