    summary:{ en:"Alicia and Will defend mountaineer Oliver Cardiff against a libel suit in London brought by a rival climber over a book describing Everest's 'death zone.' English barrister Timothy Ash Brannon, Queen's Counsel, advances the claim via letter rogatory; Alicia moves to dismiss, attacking 'libel tourism' and invoking qualified privilege, while Peter Florrick weighs retaining the firm for state civil work without breaching attorney-client privilege. The court dismisses the suit. Meanwhile Glenn Childs's past RICO exposure hangs over the firm.", zh:"艾丽西亚与威尔在伦敦为登山家奥利弗·卡迪夫辩护，后者因回忆录描述珠峰“死亡禁区”被 rival 登山者提起诽谤之诉。英格兰出庭律师、女王法律顾问蒂莫西·阿什·布兰南经调查委托书推进诉讼；艾丽西亚以“诽谤旅游”并援引合格特权申请驳回，彼得·弗洛里克则考量在不违反律师—委托人特权下将州政府民事案件交予该所。法院最终驳回起诉。与此同时，格伦·蔡尔德斯昔日的 RICO 风险悬于律所之上。" },
