    sceneNote:{ en:"The scenes move between a London courtroom and the firm's strategy sessions, highlighting the English procedural devices that differ from U.S. practice.", zh:"本集台词横跨伦敦法庭与律所策略会议，集中呈现（libel）诽谤、（libel tourism）诽谤旅游、（deposition）庭外证言、（letter rogatory）调查委托书、（Queen's Counsel）女王法律顾问、（writ）令状、（qualified privilege）合格特权、（burden of proof）举证责任、（attorney-client privilege）律师—委托人特权、（super-injunction）超级禁言令与（RICO）RICO 指控等制度。核心争点为跨国诽谤管辖、合格特权抗辩及取证方式差异。" },
    terms:[ "libel", "libel_tourism", "deposition", "letter_rogatory", "queen's_counsel", "writ", "attorney_client_privilege", "qualified_privilege", "burden_of_proof", "super_injunction", "plaintiff", "RICO" ],
    uk:{ en:"In England & Wales defamation is a tort in which the defendant traditionally bore the burden of proving truth and qualified privilege, contrary to the U.S. rule requiring a public-figure claimant to prove falsity and actual malice. 'Libel tourism' drew the Defamation Act 2013, imposing a serious-harm threshold and a forum test (s.9) so claimants must show England is clearly the most appropriate forum. 'Super-injunctions' and Queen's Counsel are distinctively English. England uses witness statements and cross-examination rather than U.S.-style depositions; a letter rogatory mirrors mutual legal assistance. RICO has no English equivalent -- rackets are prosecuted as conspiracy or specific offenses.", zh:"在英格兰与威尔士，诽谤属侵权，被告传统上须就真实性与合格特权承担举证责任，与美国要求公众人物原告证明虚假及实际恶意相反。“诽谤旅游”催生《2013年诽谤法》，确立严重损害门槛与管辖测试（第9条），原告须证明英格兰显然为最适当法院。超级禁言令与女王法律顾问为英格兰特有。英格兰以书面证词与交叉询问取代美式庭外证言；调查委托书对应司法协助。英国无 RICO 对应制度，集团犯罪以共谋或具体罪名追诉。" }
