    sceneNote:{ en:"The episode strings together several doctrines: a judge compels mediation to clear his docket; parties shelter candid advice behind attorney-client privilege and retain temporary counsel and outside counsel; a deposition is quoted to prove fraud; and the state's attorney declines fraud charges after a fraud investigation. These mechanics drive the settlement.", zh:"本集串联多项程序制度：法官以法院命令启动调解（mediation）以清理积案；当事人借律师—委托人特权（attorney-client privilege）保护坦诚意见，并聘任临时律师（temporary counsel）与外部律师（outside counsel）；通过引用庭外证词（deposition）证明欺诈（fraud）；州检察官（state's attorney）在欺诈调查（fraud investigation）后决定不提起欺诈指控（fraud charges）。这些程序机制共同推动了最终和解。" },
    terms:[ "mediation", "attorney_client_privilege", "fraud", "deposition", "temporary_counsel", "outside_counsel", "states_attorney", "blame_the_victim_defense", "fraud_investigation", "subpoena" ],
    uk:{ en:"In England and Wales, mediation is encouraged but not generally compellable. Although Churchill v Merthyr Tydfil CBC (2023) confirmed courts may lawfully order parties to mediate, referral stays discretionary and no one can be coerced into settling, unlike the episode's directive 'court-ordered mediation.' Legal professional privilege there divides into legal advice and litigation privilege, sometimes broader than U.S. attorney-client privilege. There is no elected 'state's attorney'; fraud is prosecuted by the CPS or SFO. 'Temporary' and 'outside counsel' map only loosely to solicitors and external barristers.", zh:"在英格兰与威尔士，调解受鼓励但一般不可强制；尽管 Churchill v Merthyr Tydfil CBC (2023) 确认法院可合法指令当事人调解，但转介仍属裁量事项，无人可被强迫和解——与该集指令式的「法院命令调解」不同。当地法律职业特权分为法律意见特权与诉讼特权，有时宽于美国的律师—委托人特权。英格兰与威尔士无民选「州检察官」，欺诈由皇家检控署（CPS）或欺诈调查局（SFO）追诉；「临时律师」「外部律师」仅大致对应事务律师与外部大律师。" }
